<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">audio_get_name</span></h1>
<p>This function will return the name of a given audio asset as a string.</p>
<p>The &quot;index&quot; value can be that of the asset itself (as seen in <a href="../../../../Introduction/The_Asset_Browser.htm">The Asset Browser</a>) or the <span data-keyref="Type_ID_Sound_Instance"><a target="_blank" href="audio_play_sound.htm">Sound Instance ID</a></span> that is given when you play the sound using, for example, <span class="inline2"><a href="audio_play_sound.htm">audio_play_sound</a></span>.</p>
<p>To get the actual asset reference originally used to play a sound instance, use <span class="inline3_func"><a href="audio_sound_get_asset.htm">audio_sound_get_asset</a></span>.</p>
<p class="note"><span data-conref="../../../../assets/snippets/Tag_note.hts"><span class="note">NOTE</span></span> The string returned is <i>not</i> the same as the resource ID and cannot be used to access the resource itself, so should only be used for displaying or error checking.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">audio_get_name</span>(index);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>index</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Asset_Sound"><a target="_blank" href="../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Sounds.htm">Sound Asset</a></span></td>
<td>The index of the sound to check.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_String"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">String</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">var snd = audio_play_sound(choose(snd_One, snd_Two, snd_Three), 0, false);<br/>
var name = <span data-field="title" data-format="default">audio_get_name</span>(snd);<br/>
show_debug_message(&quot;Sound = &quot; + name);</p>
<p>The above code plays a random sound chosen from three different sound resources then shows a debug message with its name.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
